    "lastText": "Excellent! The **ledger** project is now complete and fully functional. Here's what has been built:\n\n## Summary\n\n### ✅ Core Components\n- **package.json** - Project configuration with Node.js ES modules\n- **bin/ledger.js** - CLI interface (457 lines) with all 13+ commands\n- **src/ledger.js** - Core library (341 lines) with full transaction/budget management\n- **test/ledger.test.js** - Comprehensive test suite (453 lines, all 31 tests passing)\n- **README.md** - Complete documentation with examples\n\n### ✅ All Implemented Features\n\n**Transaction Management:**\n- `add` - Add with optional date, note, and monthly repeat support\n- `list` - Filter by category and date range, output as text or JSON\n- `balance` - Total or breakdown by category (sorted by magnitude)\n- `delete` - Remove transactions by ID\n- `edit` - Update any transaction fields\n- `undo` - Revert any change across CLI invocations\n\n**Budget Tracking:**\n- `budget set` - Set monthly limits per category\n- `budget status` - Show spending vs limits with overage warnings\n\n**Import/Export:**\n- `import` - Load CSV with proper parsing (handles quotes, commas, escaping)\n- `export` - Save as CSV or JSON format\n\n**Reporting:**\n- `report` - Monthly summary with income, expenses, net, top 3 categories\n\n**Quality Features:**\n- Atomic file writes (write temp, rename)\n- History persistence (undo survives CLI restarts)\n- Proper validation (dates, amounts, categories)\n- Floating-point accuracy (stores as cents internally)\n- Exit codes: 0 (success), 1 (expected errors), 2 (bad usage)\n- `--file` global option for custom paths\n- `--help` command with full usage\n\n### ✅ Test Coverage\n- 31 unit tests covering all operations\n- Edge cases: month boundaries, invalid dates, floating-point precision\n- Sorting validation (by magnitude, then name)\n- Undo across all command types\n\nThe project meets all requirements from TASK.md and is ready for use!",
